## Olive Green and Deep Forest Tones

Green gets left off most <strong>fall nail colors</strong> lists, filed under "seasonal novelty" alongside pumpkin orange and rarely taken seriously as a neutral. That undersells it. A dark, muted olive works the same way a good forest-green coat does. It is not the colour you expected to love, and then you put it on and it just makes sense.

Olive and deep forest green are having a real moment this year, largely because they photograph as moody and cool rather than Christmas-adjacent, so long as you steer clear of anything too bright or true-green. Matte finishes suit this shade family particularly well. The lack of shine keeps it looking intentional and editorial rather than like an odd colour choice.

It suits a wide range of skin tones, though richer or deeper complexions get the most drama out of it, since the green reads as jewel-toned rather than muddy against darker skin. Ask for "olive" or "deep forest," matte finish specifically, and pair it with rust, mustard, or camel in your outfit for a colour-matched autumn look rather than a clash.

