## Plum and Moody Purple

Plum is burgundy's cooler, slightly more grown-up sibling, muted and moody in a way that somehow works with just about every fall outfit you own, blazers and oversized knits included. It is the shade for anyone who wants a moody manicure without committing to actual black nails, sitting somewhere between deep purple and near-black, occasionally shifting tone depending on the light.

That colour-shift quality is exactly what makes plum more interesting than a flat black would be. It is dark enough to feel like a statement but never so opaque that it looks like you just painted your nails with a marker.

Matte is the finish to ask for here specifically. A glossy plum can look like an ordinary purple, while a matte plum-black reads as intentional and editorial. Most salons will know this shade family as "plum-black" or "vampy" by now, so you do not need to overexplain it. Pair it with deep jewel tones or an all-black outfit for a cohesive, moody look, or let it sit as the one dark note against a lighter palette.

